==================================================================
DAY 41 - PART A: THEORY
A Troubleshooting Method: Pod -> Node -> Control Plane -> Network
Time: 40 minutes
==================================================================

1. THE METHOD
-------------
Work from the symptom inward, one layer at a time. Don't guess.

  1. APPLICATION / POD
     k get pods -o wide            status? restarts? node?
     k describe pod X              events (bottom!), conditions
     k logs X [-c c] [--previous]  app output, crash reason
     k get events --sort-by=.lastTimestamp
  2. WORKLOAD / CONFIG
     k describe deploy/rs          replicas, conditions, quota errors
     referenced ConfigMaps, Secrets, PVCs, ServiceAccounts exist?
  3. SERVICE / NETWORK
     endpointslices empty? ports right? DNS? NetworkPolicy?
  4. NODE
     k get nodes ; k describe node X   Conditions, Taints, Allocated
     on the node: systemctl status kubelet ; journalctl -u kubelet
     crictl ps -a ; crictl logs ; df -h ; free -m
  5. CONTROL PLANE
     k get pods -n kube-system
     static pod manifests, crictl logs of apiserver/etcd, certs


2. STATUS -> LIKELY CAUSE
-------------------------
  Pending              no node fits (resources, taints, affinity),
                       PVC unbound, quota, scheduler down
  ContainerCreating    image pulling, volume attach/mount, CNI error,
  (long)               Secret/ConfigMap missing
  ImagePullBackOff     wrong name/tag, private registry, no network
  CrashLoopBackOff     app exits: read logs --previous; bad command,
                       config, missing env, failing liveness, OOM
  CreateContainerConfigError  missing ConfigMap/Secret key
  Running but 0/1      readiness probe failing
  OOMKilled            memory limit too low / leak
  Evicted              node pressure
  Terminating forever  finalizers, node unreachable
  Node NotReady        kubelet down, runtime down, CNI missing, disk
                       full, certificate expired, network


3. THE KUBELET IS THE KEY ON NODES
----------------------------------
  systemctl status kubelet
  journalctl -u kubelet -f
  /var/lib/kubelet/config.yaml    kubelet settings
  /etc/kubernetes/kubelet.conf    its kubeconfig
  Common: wrong cgroup driver, swap on, containerd stopped, expired
  client cert, wrong API server address.


4. WHEN kubectl ITSELF FAILS
----------------------------
"connection refused" / "the server could not find the requested
resource" / timeouts:
  - on the control plane: sudo crictl ps -a | grep apiserver
  - sudo crictl logs <apiserver-container-id>
  - check /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml for typos
  - etcd healthy? certificates valid? disk full?
  - your kubeconfig pointing to the right server?


5. DEBUG TOOLS
--------------
  k debug -it pod/X --image=nicolaka/netshoot --target=c
       attach an ephemeral debug container to a running pod
  k debug node/worker1 -it --image=busybox:1.36
       a pod on the node with the host filesystem at /host
  k run tmp --rm -it --image=nicolaka/netshoot -- bash
  k get pod X -o yaml   (compare spec with what you think)


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- Layers: pod -> workload -> network -> node -> control plane.
- describe (events) + logs (--previous) solve most pod problems.
- journalctl -u kubelet and crictl solve most node problems.
